{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970226,"nonce":"mzqCmNCTwPbixsnjc2rC250w0XU=","title":"Parameters with a default value are not nullable: an explicit null is 0, not the default","message":"Rows: Issue7032, Issue3826, Issue2224.\n\n- tast/ast_lowering/decls/fields.rs `optional_param_type` / `lower_parameter_with_hint`: `?p = 10`\n  is typed `Int` (\"a parameter with a default keeps its basic type\"), so `def4(null)` unboxes null\n  to 0 at the call site; defaults are filled only for OMITTED arguments\n  (ir/mir/helpers/signatures.rs `fill_default_args`). Haxe passes null and the callee applies the\n  default. The only callee-side null-\u003edefault prologue is for constructors with reference params\n  (ir/mir/expr/functions.rs).\n- `?x:T` becomes `Null\u003cT\u003e` only for exactly Int/Float/Bool; an abstract over Int (`EnumFlags\u003cE\u003e`,\n  `abstract Flags(Int)`) stays non-nullable, so a missing argument reads 0 (Issue2224, upstream\n  `#if !js`).\n- `bind_skipped_optional_args` (signatures.rs) puts Int, Float and Bool in one shape, so\n  `get(8.5)` with `get(?a:Int = 2, ?b:Float = 4.25)` binds 8.5 to `a` as 8 instead of skipping\n  `a` (Float does not unify with Int). Issue3826.","files":null}]}